	"marineOps": {
    "refitOrderChanged": "The squad or its equipment changed. Review the updated order before issuing.",
    "refitIssued": "Equipment plan saved. The squad's current marines, including wounded personnel, now carry the reviewed kit.",
    "refitCompletedCopy": "Technology received, kit fitted. The Machine Shop can fit and swap any learned equipment for free. Try different plans in Equipment; find more specs through markets and mission rewards.",
    "refitTransferCopy": "Wayline can transfer one equipment package as thanks for holding their checkpoint. Compare both paths, then choose one free technology transfer. Its specs are yours permanently; the Machine Shop fits them for free. The other path can be learned later through markets or mission rewards.",
    "refitFittingCopy": "The transfer is yours permanently. Select a square to compare current and proposed equipment; hover an item for full specs. Fit learned equipment for free, including on wounded marines. Other technology remains available through markets and mission rewards.",
    "refitSquadHint": "SELECT ONE FORMATION / Wounded and understrength squads can receive equipment.",
    "refitChooseTransfer": "Choose one free transfer. Comparing paths does not learn technology or change equipment.",
    "refitChooseLearned": "Choose a squad and a learned equipment path. Machine Shop fitting is free.",
    "refitSpecialRemoved": "This plan removes the current special. You can fit learned equipment again for free.",
    "refitStationed": "This squad is stationed away from the ship. Recall it before issuing equipment.",
    "refitUnknownTechnology": "Technology not learned. Find these specs through markets or mission rewards, then fit them here for free.",
    "refitUnavailable": "This order is unavailable. Select a current squad and an available equipment path.",

    "lessonSpeaker": "CASTLE / COMPANY OFFICER",
    "lessonContinue": "CONTINUE",
    "lessonEquipment": "EQUIPMENT",
    "lessonMechLab": "MECH LAB",
    "lessonBarracks": "BARRACKS",
    "lessonHeadquarters": "HEADQUARTERS",
    "lessonBriefing": "BRIEFING",
    "lessonOpenWayward": "OPEN WAYWARD",
    "lessonReady": "READY",
    "lessonUnderstood": "UNDERSTOOD",
    "lessonRefitTitle": "A PROPER ISSUE",
    "lessonRefitHandoff": "You brought our people home, Commander. Wayline has offered one equipment package for holding the checkpoint. Come to Equipment: we will choose its technology, compare the kit, then issue it to a squad.",
    "lessonRefitSquad": "Choose the squad receiving this first issue. Wounded marines keep their billets and can receive equipment too. This changes the equipment plan; it does not replace missing soldiers.",
    "lessonRefitCompare": "Compare the two packages. Steady Line strengthens sustained fire; Forward Screen provides pulse weapons and Janus armor. Select a package, then inspect the highlighted billets to see what would change.",
    "lessonRefitClaim": "When you are satisfied, learn the selected package. This is our one free technology transfer. Its specifications stay with the company; the other package can be learned later.",
    "lessonRefitIssue": "The specifications are ours. Now issue the reviewed kit using the highlighted order. Learning a technology and equipping our people are separate steps. The Machine Shop fits learned infantry equipment for free.",
    "lessonGantryTitle": "WAYWARD AT THE GANTRY",
    "lessonGantryHandoff": "Counterattack left us a Hound, and the damaged gantry has been restored to house it. Come to the Mech Lab. We will fit its spare missile rack and practice removing and reusing hardware.",
    "lessonGantry1": "There she is: Wayward. Our first walker is a substantial increase in firepower, but she still needs infantry watching her approaches. Open her gantry and we will fit the SRM rack supplied with the recovery.",
    "lessonGantry2": "Select an empty shoulder, then install the SRM-5 spare from the catalog, or drag it onto the shoulder. Its 2 × 2 footprint fits that mount. Keep the nose chaingun fitted. We are using a physical spare from bay stores.",
    "lessonGantry3": "Now remove the fitted SRM using its remove control, or drag it back to stores. Then install that same spare again. Take your time: a refit returns usable hardware to stores; it does not destroy it.",
    "lessonGantry4": "Fit checked. The active lance answers Mech Support when the contract supplies heavy lift. Select that support in the Junction briefing; owning the walker alone will not put her on the ground. We will cover her heat and infantry screen once she lands.",
    "lessonInvestmentsTitle": "SPEND WHERE IT HELPS",
    "lessonInvestmentsCopy": "We have earned some breathing room. Engineering shows the ship repairs; the Boat Deck shows lift capacity and refits. A second bay and larger boats are useful investments, but optional. Our Hermes can make repeat trips, and Wayline supplies the heavy lift for its mech-support contract. Keep enough stores to raise and replenish the second squad.",
    "lessonFormationTitle": "FROM ONE SQUAD TO TWO",
    "lessonFormationHandoff": "Junction asks us to hold several places at once. We should bring two full squads. Let us check the Barracks, fill vacant billets and put both formations under command before choosing the deployment.",
    "lessonFormationFound": "We need another formation. Open Found Line Squad and review the real stores bill before ordering. Buy missing Marines, supplies or food at a market. Leaving to resupply is fine; I will pick up here when you return.",
    "lessonFormationAssign": "Both formations exist. Select them in Barracks and assign them from the commander card. Then open the mission briefing and include both in Assign Squads. Formation ownership, commander assignment and deployment selection are separate orders.",
    "lessonFormationRecover": "We have two formations, but fewer than two full squads ready. Fill vacant billets from reserves or consolidate fit marines; wounded soldiers keep their billets. Let them recover if needed. Assign both formations to command, then include them in the briefing deployment.",
    "lessonSecondTitle": "PREPARE A LARGER FORCE",
    "lessonSecondMinimum": "The launch minimum is two squads with four ready marines each.",
    "lessonSecondCheck": "Check this briefing’s deployment requirements before committing.",
    "lessonSecondSummary": "This operation recommends {0} marines. {1}\n\nFull squads aboard: {2}. Ready marines: {3}.\n{4}\n\nOne new squad / Cost / Available / Buy\n{5}\nFounding provides twelve soldiers and their starter kit. Learned infantry equipment can be fitted for free. Use Barracks to assign formations to a commander, then Assign Squads here to select the deployment. Wounded soldiers keep their billets.",
    "lessonSecondFull": "You already have two full squads; there is no need to raise another for this lesson.",
    "lessonSecondExisting": "Fill the vacancies in your existing formations or allow wounded soldiers to recover.",
    "lessonSecondFound": "Open Barracks, then Found Line Squad. Buy any missing stores at a market.",
    "lessonCostLine": "{0} / {1} / {2} / {3}\n",
    "lessonJunctionTitle": "PUT THE COMPANY ON THE MANIFEST",
    "lessonJunctionSquads": "Use Assign Squads to include two formations. Each needs at least four ready marines to launch; two full squads are recommended. Prepare or replenish them in Barracks if necessary. Departure is your decision, but leaving this screen does not complete the lesson.",
    "lessonJunctionSupport": "Our infantry is selected. Add Mech Support to the command deck so the active lance can join them. Remove another power if the deck is full. Wayline provides the heavy carrier for this job; buying another shuttle is not required.",
    "lessonJunctionReady": "Both formations and Mech Support are selected. Check the transport readout: infantry rides our boats, while the active mech lance uses the contracted heavy carrier. Confirm this preparation, then deploy when you are ready. In battle, select Mech Support and choose its landing point.",
    "lessonJunctionWithoutMech": "Both formations are selected. Mech Support is not available for this deployment. You can proceed with infantry; the field lesson will wait for an eligible contract with an owned mech in the active lance.",
    "lessonFieldTitle": "MECH SUPPORT ON THE GROUND",
    "lessonFieldCall": "Select Mech Support in the highlighted command tray, then choose a safe landing point. The active lance travels on that call; it does not land automatically. Keep infantry near the approach to protect the carrier.",
    "lessonFieldInbound": "The call is accepted. Keep the landing area safe while the heavy carrier comes in. We will check the walker once she is on the ground.",
    "lessonFieldLanded": "There she is. Keep infantry ahead to spot threats and protect her flanks. Chaingun and missile bursts share heat: ease off as the heat bar turns amber. Loaders cycle separately, and the replenisher restores spent missile packs. Select the walker to inspect her weapons and heat.",

